Package: dtaparser
Title: Fast Reader for Stata DTA Files
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jonathan@bearak.net")
Description: Reads Stata DTA files into tibbles with a Rust parser, multicore
    decoding, and compact in-memory representations for numeric and character
    columns. Its read interface follows 'haven' while retaining dataset labels,
    variable labels, display formats, value labels, temporal classes, and Stata
    tagged missing values. It also provides label-aware tabulation and
    tag-preserving recoding.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr (>= 1.1.0),
    readr (>= 2.2.0),
    rlang,
    tibble,
    tidyselect,
    vctrs
Suggests:
    callr,
    haven,
    httpuv,
    labelled,
    testthat (>= 3.1.7)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo and Rust >= 1.98.0; on Windows, the Rust target matching
    R (x86_64-pc-windows-gnu for x86_64 R or
    aarch64-pc-windows-gnullvm for aarch64 R)
NeedsCompilation: yes
